[SPEAKER_03]: If you were to kind of remember this whole, what somebody told you, don't take things personally, then you can take that.

48
00:04:40,182 --> 00:04:47,907
[SPEAKER_03]: You can turn the same attitude towards anything you think, anything you feel, anything you intend, here and now, and not take it personally.

49
00:04:48,387 --> 00:04:54,091
[SPEAKER_03]: Because it is always on the level of this most immediate choice slash attitude.

50
00:04:55,296 --> 00:05:05,087
[SPEAKER_03]: Whether you're going to be personally involved, or whether you're going to keep that context and perspective of, I shall not be personally involved with this situation.

51
00:05:05,168 --> 00:05:13,838
[SPEAKER_03]: So, what happens if you... what is the most general characteristic if you... when you are personally involved with the situation?

52
00:05:15,367 --> 00:05:15,927
[SPEAKER_03]: Ignoring.

53
00:05:16,168 --> 00:05:16,728
[SPEAKER_03]: Ignoring.

54
00:05:17,008 --> 00:05:18,970
[SPEAKER_03]: Loss of context.

55
00:05:19,370 --> 00:05:19,871
[SPEAKER_03]: Absorbed.

56
00:05:20,691 --> 00:05:23,293
[SPEAKER_03]: You're absorbed in the objects of your experience.

57
00:05:23,774 --> 00:05:38,765
[SPEAKER_03]: The attitude of being just absorbed into day-to-day things, in your senses, in your thoughts, and not having perspective on yourself in the situation, that's already a symptom of having taken things personally.

58
00:05:39,706 --> 00:05:39,966
[SPEAKER_03]: So,

59
00:05:40,847 --> 00:05:53,595
[SPEAKER_03]: You could be thinking about how not to take things personally, when somebody says this, somebody does that, but if you are absorbed in that, with same lack of awareness, you're taking that personally.

60
00:05:53,615 --> 00:05:55,276
[SPEAKER_03]: Of course, yes.

61
00:05:55,516 --> 00:05:56,496
[SPEAKER_03]: And that's the point here.

62
00:05:56,656 --> 00:06:09,264
[SPEAKER_03]: You recognize that all these motions, all these things you might do, are on that, kind of, they're secondary to that basic choice of, before I act by body, by speech, or by mind,

63
00:06:10,247 --> 00:06:22,753
[SPEAKER_03]: The most fundamental choice, the most fundamental direction that I have is go with it, I take it personally, refrain from it, maintain perspective, which will prevent me from taking personally as much.

64
