[SPEAKER_03]: And do do people see now what else is mirrored through this?

65
00:06:30,588 --> 00:06:31,068
[SPEAKER_03]: Anatta.

66
00:06:32,189 --> 00:06:33,731
[SPEAKER_03]: Okay, that's that's too easy.

67
00:06:35,152 --> 00:06:38,915
[SPEAKER_03]: No, no, I mean this this this like going with it or not going with it.

68
00:06:39,235 --> 00:06:40,476
[SPEAKER_03]: Oh, this has to do with the sense restraint.

69
00:06:40,516 --> 00:06:41,277
[SPEAKER_03]: Exactly, yeah.

70
00:06:41,817 --> 00:06:56,910
[SPEAKER_03]: And that's how you would start the sense restraint and keeping the precepts and virtue, because unknowingly, you're already diminishing the degree of taking things personally, even if you don't actually know anything about personality or not taking things personally, never heard an anatta and so on.

71
00:07:00,739 --> 00:07:07,803
[SPEAKER_03]: That's why people can understand the attitude of not taking things personally, and they can do it to a degree.

72
00:07:08,564 --> 00:07:21,431
[SPEAKER_03]: But if their behavior is not developed, if their choices and actions are not purified, it's going to work for a few moments, for as much as you have developed your composure, which means very little.

73
00:07:21,551 --> 00:07:22,732
[SPEAKER_03]: And then it will become abstract.

74
00:07:22,772 --> 00:07:28,295
[SPEAKER_03]: It will become that secondary psychologization of, you know, taking things personally while everything is taken personally here and now.

75
00:07:30,393 --> 00:07:47,313
[SPEAKER_03]: And that's because the actions rooted in greed, lust, sensuality, desire, aversion, ill will, annoyance, distraction, delusion, indolence, ignorance, all of those attitudes are attitudes that are

