[SPEAKER_01]: When it describes, you know, sense restraint and guarding the sense doors, which is kind of what would come on top of that, is, like, could basically nearly be summarized by saying, don't be absorbed in what your eyes see, what you're... when seeing a sight with the eyes, when hearing

